}", "memory.md": "Closing steps. A request often ends with a closing step after the main update. Do it before you finish:
- When it ends by asking you to post a message in a Slack channel, make that post: use the channel the request names and the text it gives.
- When it ends by asking you to tag the contact, add that tag to the contact.
"}, "targets": {"worker.system_prompt": {"binding": "config", "kinds": ["prompt"], "site": "agent.system_prompt"}, "worker.finish": {"binding": "config", "kinds": ["prompt", "workflow"], "site": "agent.system_prompt.finish_check", "current": "Before you report the task as finished, re-read the request and check every requirement it states, including any at the end. For each one, name the tool result that shows it is done. If one is missing, do it now instead of finishing."}, "worker.stop": {"binding": "decision", "kinds": ["rule", "model"], "site": "stop.on_finish"}, "worker.harness": {"binding": "config", "kinds": ["workflow"], "site": "agent.harness_package"}}, "experience": [{"kind": "experiment", "outcome": "rejected", "installed": false, "hypothesis": "Naming follow-up tasks in the closing-steps working note makes the agent create them, as naming posts and tags did.", "targets": ["worker.harness"], "metrics": {"gain": 0.0, "regression_rate": 0.0}}, {"kind": "diagnosis", "noted": 1, "failures": 2, "reused": 0, "measured": 3, "passed": 1}, {"kind": "experiment", "outcome": "accepted", "installed": true, "hypothesis": "The agent skips closing steps its working note does not name; naming tagging in the closing-steps note fixes requests that end with a tag.", "targets": ["worker.harness"], "metrics": {"gain": 0.166667, "regression_rate": 0.0}}, {"kind": "diagnosis", "noted": 1, "failures": 3, "reused": 0, "measured": 4, "passed": 1}, {"kind": "experiment", "outcome": "accepted", "installed": true, "hypothesis": "The agent skips closing Slack posts because no instruction covers them; a working note that says to make the post fixes this class of request.", "targets": ["worker.harness"], "metrics": {"gain": 0.166667, "regression_rate": 0.0}}, {"kind": "diagnosis", "noted": 1, "failures": 4, "reused": 0, "measured": 7, "passed": 3}, {"kind": "round", "outcome": "infrastructure_failed"}], "budget": {"remaining": {"usd": 45.0}, "used": {}}, "notes": [{"task_id": "marketing.reh_002", "note_ref": "note:sha256:3b0f94c478886b7cc7ed89982da12b75c4453cd1683fe4a92df63a85ed6a15d1", "component": "memory", "failure_class": "closing step skipped", "generality": "Same class as the skipped closing post and tag: the agent stops after the main update whenever the closing step is of a kind its note does not name. Naming follow-up tasks covers every request that ends with one.", "mechanism": "Extend the working note on closing steps: when a request ends by asking to log a follow-up task for the contact, create that task with the title the request gives before finishing.", "root_cause": "The agent made the main update and finished. The request ended with a closing step, logging a follow-up task for the contact, and the agent's last message says nothing in its instructions covers closing steps of this kind. The only failed check is the follow-up task."}]}
